 "Absurd and surreal":["A cloud asked the moon for directions. The moon said, ‘Just follow the tide.’ The cloud got very wet.", "Two antennas got married. The ceremony was dull, but the reception was excellent.", "A sandwich walks into a bar. The bartender says, ‘Sorry, we don’t serve food here.’", "Two fish are in a tank. One says to the other, ‘Do you know how to drive this thing?’", "A man walks into a library and asks for a book on paranoia. The librarian whispers, ‘It’s right behind you.’", "A grape walks into a bar and orders a drink. The bartender asks, ‘Why the long face?’ The grape says, ‘I’m a raisin.’", "My cat speaks four languages. Mostly meow, but with feeling.", "I asked the lamp for advice. It said, ‘Lighten up.’ Then it switched itself off.", "The past, the present and the future walked into a bar. It was tense.", "A beat walked into a bar. Then another bar. Then two more. That was a phrase."],
 "Wholesome":["What did the bee say to the flower? Hey, bud, you’re looking great today.", "What did one plate say to the other? Dinner’s on me.", "Why did the sun never go to college? It already had a million degrees and so do you.", "What did the big flower say to the small flower? Hey, bud!", "What do you call a hug from a bear? Unbearably sweet.", "Why did the cookie cry? Its mother had been a wafer so long.", "What did the stamp say to the envelope? Stick with me and we’ll go places.", "Why are friends like stars? You don’t always see them, but you know they’re there.", "What did the ocean say to the sailor? Nothing, it just waved hello.", "What did the battery say to the phone? I’ve got you, every day."],
